title: Bayern Landtag Election
subtitle:
view-if: year = 1970 and month == 11
frequency: 1000
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival:
set-jump: post_election_1970_ba
tags: event

= Bayern Landtag Election

The Landtag of Bayern is getting elected.

- @election_algorithm: May we do our best...

@post_election_1970_ba
on-arrival: {!
var ba_adjustment_factors = {
    spd: 0.8,
    cdu: 1.3,
    fdp: 0.9,
    npd: 1.0,
    other: 1.0,
};

var new_party_sum = 0;
for (var party of Q.parties) {
    Q.spd_ba = Q.spd_votes*ba_adjustment_factors.spd;
    Q.cdu_ba = Q.cdu_votes*ba_adjustment_factors.cdu;
    Q.fdp_ba = Q.fdp_votes*ba_adjustment_factors.fdp;
    Q.npd_ba = Q.npd_votes*ba_adjustment_factors.npd;
    Q.other_ba = Q.other_votes*ba_adjustment_factors.other;

    if (Q[party + '_votes'] < 5 || party == 'other' || Q[party + '_banned']) {
        Q[party + '_ba'] = 0;
    }

    new_party_sum += Q[party + '_ba'];
}
// calculate new party sum if electoral reform
for (var party of Q.parties) {
    if (Q[party + '_ba'] > 0) {
        Q[party + '_ba'] = Math.round(Q[party + '_ba']*1000/new_party_sum)/10;
    }
}

// get change arrows and signs


// The largest party can only be the CSU or the SPD.
Q.largest_party = 'SPD';
if (Q.cdu_ba >= Q.spd_ba) {
    Q.largest_party_ba = 'CSU';
}

// coalitions
Q.social_liberal_coalition_ba = Q.spd_ba + Q.fdp_ba;
Q.grand_coalition_ba = Q.spd_ba + Q.cdu_ba;
Q.bourgeois_coalition_ba = Q.fdp_ba + Q.cdu_ba;

var election_result = {'date': new Date(Q.year, Q.month - 1)};
for (var party of Q.parties) {
    election_result[party] = Q[party + '_ba'];
}
Q.election_records.push(election_result);
!}
on-departure:
on-display: {!
data = []
data.push({
      "id": "spd",
      "legend": "SPD",
      "name": "SPD",
      "seats": Math.round(Q.spd_ba*2),
});
data.push({
      "id": "fdp",
      "legend": "FDP",
      "name": "FDP",
      "seats": Math.round(Q.fdp_ba*2),
});
data.push({
      "id": "csu",
      "legend": "CSU",
      "name": "CSU",
      "seats": Math.round(Q.cdu_ba*2),
});
data.push({
      "id": "npd",
      "legend": "NPD",
      "name": "NPD",
      "seats": Math.round(Q.npd_ba*2),
});
data.push({
      "id": "other",
      "legend": "Other",
      "name": "Other",
      "seats": Math.round(Q.other_ba*2),
});

if (window && d3) {
    var width = 500; 
    var height = 500;
    var screenWidth = document.getElementById('content').offsetWidth;
    if (screenWidth < width - 50) {
        width = screenWidth - 50; 
        height = width;
        document.getElementById("reichstag").style.height = screenWidth/2 + "px";
    } 

    var parliament = d3.parliament();
    parliament.width(width).height(height).innerRadiusCoef(0.4);
    parliament.enter.fromCenter(true).smallToBig(true);
    parliament.exit.toCenter(false).bigToSmall(true);
    d3.select("#reichstag").datum(data).call(parliament);
}
!}
go-to: coalition_menu

= Election results

{!<svg id="reichstag" style="width: 500px; height: 250px;"> </svg>!}

{!<table>!} 
{!<tr><td>Party</td><td>Vote share</td>!}
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#C00000; outline: 2px; outline-style: solid;'> </div> !} **SPD:** {!</td><td>!} **[+ spd_ba +]%**

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#286fe0'> </div> !} CSU: {!</td><td>!} [+ cdu_ba +]% {!</td><td>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#FFCC00'> </div> !} FDP: {!</td><td>!} [+ fdp_ba +]% {!</td><td>!}
 
{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#a0a0a0'> </div> !} Others: {!</td><td>!} [+ other_ba +] % {!</td><td>!}

{!<tr><td><div class="box" style='background-color:#c26f2b'> </div> !} NPD: {!</td><td>!} [+ npd_ba +]% {!</td><td>!}
{!</table>!}

**Potential coalitions:**

<span style="color: #C00000;">Social</span>-<span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberal</span> Coalition (<span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> + <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span>): [+ social_liberal_coalition_ba +]%

<span style="color: #C00000;">Grand</span> <span style="color: #286fe0;">Coalition</span> (<span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> + <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span>: [+ grand_coalition_ba +]%

<span style="color: #FFCC00;">Bour</span><span style="color: #286fe0;">geois</span> Coalition (<span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> + <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span>): [+ bourgeois_coalition_ba +]%

There are some potential coalition arrangements.

@coalition_menu

- @spd_majority
- @csu_majority
- @social_liberal_coalition
- @grand_coalition
- @bourgeois_coalition

@csu_majority
title: A <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> majority alone
subtitle: <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span>: [+ cdu_ba +]%
view-if: cdu_ba >= 50
on-arrival: ba_leader = "Goppel"; ba_leader_party = "CSU"; ba_coalition = "CSU majority"; ba_next_election = "Oktober 1974"

The <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> has formed a majority government...

@bourgeois_coalition
title: A <span style="color: #FFCC00;">Bour</span><span style="color: #286fe0;">geois</span> Coalition is formed.
subtitle: <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> + <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> + <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span> ([+ bourgeois_coalition_ba +]%)
view-if: bourgeois_coalition_ba >= 50
choose-if: cdu_ba <= 50
unavailable-subtitle: [? if cdu_ba >= 50: The <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> does not need a coalition partner. ?]
on-arrival: ba_leader = "Goppel"; ba_leader_party = "CSU"; ba_coalition = "Bourgeois Coalition"; ba_next_election = "Oktober 1974"

For some reason, we cannot or do not want to form a government. This has led to the <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> forming a coalition with the <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span>.

@spd_majority
title: A <span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> majority alone
subtitle: <span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span>: [+ spd_ba +]%
view-if: spd_ba >= 50
on-arrival: ba_leader = "Gabert"; ba_leader_party = "SPD"; ba_coalition = "SPD majority"; ba_next_election = "Oktober 1974"
achievement: majority_party

Finally, the <span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> can govern alone! Our long campaign of electioneering has paid off. We do not need to worry about coalition government; anything is possible.

@social_liberal_coalition
title: We can form a <span style="color: #C00000;">Social</span>-<span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberal</span> Coalition.
subtitle: <span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> + <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span> ([+ social_liberal_coalition_ba +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: [? if fdp_relation < 60: The <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span> does not want to form a coalition with us. ?]
view-if: social_liberal_coalition_ba >= 50
choose-if: fdp_relation >= 60
on-arrival: ba_leader = "Gabert"; ba_leader_party = "SPD"; ba_coalition = "Social-liberal Coalition"; ba_next_election = "Oktober 1974"

We have enough votes to form a <span style="color: #C00000;">Social</span>-<span style="color: #FFCC00;">liberal</span> Coalition government consisting of the <span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> and <span style="color: #FFCC00;">**FDP**</span>!

@grand_coalition
title: We can form a <span style="color: #C00000;">Grand</span> <span style="color: #286fe0;">Coalition</span>.
view-if: grand_coalition_ba >= 50
choose-if: cdu_relation >= 60 and cdu_ba <= 50
subtitle: <span style="color: #C00000;">**SPD**</span> + <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> ([+ grand_coalition_ba +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: [? if cdu_relation < 60: The <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> does not want to form a coalition with us. ?][? if cdu_ba >= 50: The <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span> does not need a coalition partner. ?]
on-arrival: ba_leader = "Gabert" if largest_party_ba == "SPD"; ba_leader = "Goppel" if largest_party_ba == "CSU"; ba_leader_party = "SPD" if largest_party_ba == "SPD"; ba_leader_party = "CSU" if largest_party_ba == "CSU"; ba_coalition = "Grand Coalition"; ba_next_election = "Oktober 1974"

We have formed a Coalition with the <span style="color: #286fe0;">**CSU**</span>.
